  "title": "what a delegated lane's isolation actually buys, per platform",
  "source": "code-read",
  "source_detail": "protocol/lanes.md:76-92 for the flags and the verified port-binding failure; Claude Code and Codex Windows docs for what each enforces there; Q1 of this plan",
  "explanation": "The arrow to look at is the short one from the sandbox question straight to a confident report with nothing behind it: that path already exists on Linux, was hit for real there, and is the reason the flags are requests rather than guarantees. Windows widens it rather than creating it, which is why [the three ways out](#the-call) differ in what they document, not in what they can promise. Leaves out which stages delegate at all, and leaves out Claude's own lane, which takes no flags either way.",
